 ## Operating characteristics
--   **Correctness:** Guarantees topological correctness for surfaces satisfying the interval condition, unlike original MC [S1].
--   **Complexity:** Linear in the number of grid cells. Each cell is processed independently.
--   **Limitations:** Requires the interval condition to hold. If the surface is too complex or the grid too coarse, the condition may fail, leading to discarded cells or incorrect topology if not handled. The method assumes single intersections per edge [S1].
--   **Performance:** Placing vertices at edge centers is computationally cheaper than linear interpolation, though it may reduce geometric accuracy slightly.
