 ## Background
-The method was introduced in "Isotopic approximation of implicit curves and surfaces" [S1]. It builds on the original Marching Cubes by Lorensen and Cline [LC87] but modifies the vertex placement and ambiguity resolution to ensure isotopic equivalence (topological correctness). It is often used as a precursor to octree-based meshing algorithms.
